Answer: No, Pennsylvania election officials did not reject 372,000 cast mail-in ballots; rather, they rejected 372,000 "requests for mail ballots" (ballot applications). According to the provided report, "More than 90% of those applications, or about 336,000, were denied as duplicates," primarily because voters who had already requested mail-in ballots for the state's June primary did not realize they had already opted to automatically receive them for the general election as well.

